From 3a71e1cc4dc11f6ea5340ce3e194b702f2c63de5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Esteban Ordano <42750+eordano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Honour _NET_WM_OPAQUE_REGION: give the surface the window's
 opaque region

Chromium (and other X11 clients) set _NET_WM_OPAQUE_REGION on their windows,
but the region never reached the host compositor, which therefore had to draw
everything beneath every X11 window and blend it. The property is now read when
a window's properties are read and on every change or delete, converted from
window pixels to surface units (clipped to the window, rounded inwards so no
pixel the client does not draw opaque is claimed), and given to the surface
with its next commit, again only when the region, the window size or the scale
changed.
---
